 "note": "`reproduced_exactly` records whether this port rebuilds the input tensor bit for bit. Where it is false the cause is the cubic resize's measured residual divergence from OpenCV, documented in src/resize_cubic.rs and docs/LAYOUT_CONTRACT.md; the field exists so the divergence is asserted and bounded rather than hidden. This capture is schema v2: it executes the pinned PaddleX operators rather than transcribing them, which is what exposed the two bugs v1 encoded -- a BGR source where upstream reads RGB, and a division by 255 where upstream multiplies by a folded 1/255.",
